# CrewPulse: rules for AI assistants

(This same file is copied to AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/project.mdc and .github/copilot-instructions.md so every tool reads it.)

## What we are building
An Event Volunteer & Crowd Coordination Platform. **Read PRD.md before any task.**
The core challenge is the assignment engine in `src/lib/engine`. Hackathon: ship a polished, working demo in ~4.5 hours.
Speed beats perfection, but the demo path (see PRD "Demo script") must never break.

## Stack (fixed, do not change, do not add frameworks)
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind + shadcn/ui
- Supabase (Postgres + Realtime) via `@supabase/supabase-js`
- Framer Motion (animation), Recharts (charts), lucide-react (icons), sonner (toasts)
- SWR (data fetching), zod + react-hook-form (forms), date-fns (dates), @dnd-kit (drag and drop)
- vitest for engine unit tests
- NO Python, NO separate backend, NO ORM, NO Redux. Logic lives in Next.js route handlers and `src/lib/engine`.
- Do not `npm install` anything new without asking the human. `package.json` is owned by P4.

